From 5ca49b496f388cb16ca3fd5cf5c6e3f40a8a94f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(widget): show the scroll bars only while scrolling on iOS
 and Android

scrollBarAlwaysVisible was true everywhere but macOS, so on a phone every
list carried its bar for good, a dark 6 px rail on the right edge. The
native lists of both systems show it only while the content moves.

On iOS and Android the bars now use the scrolling state that macOS overlay
scroll bars already had: a drag shows them, they stay while the finger is
down (even if it rests), and they hide scrollEndDelay after the drag ends
unless another one starts. Desktop behaviour is unchanged, macOS included.
New tests cover showing, staying, hiding and a drag that cancels the hide,
and that the desktop never enters the scrolling state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
